		"complexity": 3,
		"description": "<p>Rusty scrap and a pile of junk is useless to most, but you see an opportunity. While others spend years perfecting their footwork or praying to silent gods, you're busy with a wrench and a bucket of gears. Why wait for a miracle when you can build one yourself?</p><p>To be an Engineer is to look at a problem and realize you have exactly three different ways to blow it up in your pocket. You don't just participate in a fight. You renovate the battlefield. Your power isn't a gift or a secret. It is something you forged with your own two hands. You are the master of the \"what-if.\" You are the person who brought a gun to a sword fight, then decided to add a self-firing turret just to be safe.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Turrets.</strong> Deploy specialized turrets to automate the destruction of your enemies and provide cover for your team.</p></li><li><p><strong>Gadgets.</strong> Spend Toolbelt scraps to activate custom inventions, giving you the perfect tool for every disaster.</p></li><li><p><strong>Weapon Kits.</strong> Use specialized \"kits\" designed by you to outplay your opponents and keep them guessing!</p></li></ul>",
